# zcomp

- Label: Z Composite
- Category: Copernicus (`Cop`), Houdini 22.0.368
- Inputs: 1 to 4
- Parameters: 3 (exact, read from Houdini by hython)
- Used by the height graph: no

## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/zcomp.html
- Summary (EN): Z Composite combines two layers according to their depth, placing the closer pixel in front of the farther one. Output: the composite layer with combined depth.
- Résumé (FR) : Compose deux couches selon leur profondeur, en plaçant le pixel le plus proche devant l'autre, avec gestion de la conversion de profondeur et de l'offset anti-z-fighting.

- Inputs meaning: ["bg: background layer; sets the output size and resolution; if it has the lower depth it is placed over fg instead", "bgdepth: per-pixel depth of the background layer", "fg: nominal foreground layer; if it has the greater depth it is placed behind bg instead", "fgdepth: per-pixel depth of the foreground layer"]

- Key parameters: ["Signature: the layer type the source accepts", "Convert Depth: how input depth layers are read; Depth and Distance treat zero as infinity and increase away from the camera; Height has no special zero and increases toward the camera; the combined depth output keeps the input's type", "FG Offset: biases foreground depth toward the camera to prevent z-fighting when both share a depth; does not affect the output depth"]

- Caveats: ["An ID layer cannot be blended, so the node outputs the ID value of the lowest-depth pixel instead"]

